      "Most new account forms include a predispute arbitration agreement. The customer agrees to settle any dispute with the firm through arbitration instead of court. No rule says a customer must sign one. But nearly every firm requires it, because arbitration is cheaper and faster.\n\nIf a firm uses one, FINRA requires it to be highlighted and to explain that:\n• The customer is giving up the right to sue\n• Arbitration is final and binding\n• Arbitrators do not have to explain the reasons for their award\n• Arbitration panels include a minority of people who are or were in the securities industry\n\nIf the customer signs, a standalone copy must be sent to the customer, and the customer must sign an acknowledgment of receipt within 30 days.",
