      "Customers may open a numbered account, using a number or symbol instead of a name so they stay anonymous when trading. The firm must still record the customer's identity on the new account form, and the owner must sign the form plus a statement saying they own the account. Both must be kept on file.\n\nCustomers may also open several individual accounts at one firm, but must sign a statement that the accounts are not for anyone else.\n\nA copy of the new account form must be sent to the customer:\n• Within 30 days of opening the account\n• At least every 36 months after that, to verify and update information\n• Within 30 days of any updates\n\nIf a rep learns of a change in material facts, the rep must check with the customer before changing the account form.\n\nCustomer records must be kept at least 6 years after the information was last updated and at least 6 years after the account is closed.",
